   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fab977c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Interpretation.** All models find *sadness* and *joy* easiest, the two largest classes (581 and 695 test texts). The minority classes separate the rungs: *surprise* rises from 0.36 (Naive Bayes, whose additive smoothing gives the rare class little probability mass) to 0.69 with logistic regression and 0.78 with BERT, and *love* from 0.59 to 0.85. BERT's gains over TF-IDF + LR are largest exactly there (+0.088 for both *love* and *surprise*) and smallest for *joy* (+0.034). Because macro-F1 weights every class equally, these two minority classes account for a large part of the difference in macro-F1 between the rungs. GloVe + LR is weak in every class, not only in the rare ones: averaging hurts the representation itself, not just the class balance."
   ]
  },
